      "target_path": "specification/dynamodb-encryption-client/encrypt-item.md",
      "target_section": "parsed-header",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When ordering strings,\nthese strings MUST be compared according to their UTF-16 encoding,\nlexicographically per [UTF-16 code unit](#utf-16-code-unit).\n",
      "id": "1ab6d9a15a6b153d",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 26,
      "quote": "When ordering strings, these strings MUST be compared according to their UTF-16 encoding, lexicographically per [UTF-16 code unit](#utf-16-code-unit).",
      "source": "compliance/specification/dynamodb-encryption-client/string-ordering/utf-16-binary-order.toml",
      "target_path": "specification/dynamodb-encryption-client/string-ordering.md",
      "target_section": "utf-16-binary-order",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "UTF-16 code units for [high or low surrogates](#surrogates) MUST be compared individually,\nand the [Unicode scalar value](#unicode-scalar-value) represented by a surrogate pair\nMUST NOT be compared.\n",
      "id": "67ee1141772d5a56",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 34,
      "quote": "UTF-16 code units for [high or low surrogates](#surrogates) MUST be compared individually, and the [Unicode scalar value](#unicode-scalar-value) represented by a surrogate pair MUST NOT be compared.",
      "source": "compliance/specification/dynamodb-encryption-client/string-ordering/utf-16-binary-order.toml",
      "target_path": "specification/dynamodb-encryption-client/string-ordering.md",
      "target_section": "utf-16-binary-order",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Specifically, the range of characters with Unicode code point U+E000 to U+0xFFFF\n(code points representable by 16 bits, but after the surrogate range)\nMUST be considered \"greater than\" any character with a Unicode code point of U+10000 to U+10FFFF.\n",
      "id": "dbe569fc1100655b",
      "level": "Must",
      "line": 42,
      "quote": "Specifically, the range of characters with Unicode code point U+E000 to U+0xFFFF (code points representable by 16 bits, but after the surrogate range) MUST be considered \"greater than\" any character with a Unicode code point of U+10000 to U+10FFFF.",
      "source": "compliance/specification/dynamodb-encryption-client/string-ordering/utf-16-binary-order.toml",
      "target_path": "specification/dynamodb-encryption-client/string-ordering.md",
      "target_section": "utf-16-binary-order",
      "type": "SPEC"
    },
    {
